                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Oral Anatomy and Physiology is a crucial discipline within dental medicine and serves as a core course in oral medical majors. It is an integrative field that closely combines foundational knowledge with clinical practice. The subject systematically explores the morphological structures and physiological functions of teeth, occlusion, jaws, and the skull, along with their underlying principles. It further bridges oral function with clinical applications while introducing advancements from both domestic and international research. This course lays a necessary foundation for studying other fundamental and clinical oral medicine courses, as well as providing a solid basis for future clinical dental practice.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
